== held-out definitions in the repo (which set each number used) ==
  HO1000  runs/*/rr/dev_scored.jsonl: 1,000 v3-covered, plan-rendered gold, retail_world (40) in. All rows above.
  HO960   HO1000 minus retail_world: R2 first 59.58, validator 66.46, oracle 70.31 (about -1.0 vs HO1000).
  HO-train1455 / HO-A1395  training-time greedy evals (train_sq2.py), paired only with the training GATE (first pick on 1,297 covered dev, uncovered wrong); 5-checkpoint Spearman +0.70 mixes three definitions.
  ho200 / ho154  ORIGINAL train gold, Mac int8 decode: R2 greedy 53.90 on 154 valid vs dev200 46.94 on 196.
  v2 decision/reserved (data/sys1/heldout_v2): ORIGINAL gold, all executable questions incl. 16% v3-uncovered, no retail_world. A System-1 pipeline with no fallback scores 0 on uncovered items, so v2 ~= HO960 x 960/1144 (= 0.839 x HO960) for such systems: R2 first pick 48.74 on the decision set (scripts/analysis/heldout_v2.py score).

Reading: on HO1000 the plain offset (dev ~= held-out -11.74, residual SD 1.41) is as good as the line (slope 0.96); predicting a new system's dev level from held-out carries about +-2 points (leave-one-system-out RMSE up to 2.1 for the offset, worst on D0, whose dev rows mix GPU and Mac-int8 decodes). Across systems, held-out deltas map to dev deltas with a median ratio near 1.3 but a range that includes sign flips; a held-out delta below ~1 point does not predict the sign of the dev delta. Re-fit on v2 once systems are scored on it.
